          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the heaviest job your property needs, then choose the size class, weight and hitch category that handle it. For most two-to-five-acre properties, a sub-compact such as the Kubota BX23S, John Deere 1025R or Kioti CS2520 is the right tool, with the BX23S the pick if digging is on the list. For larger properties with pasture and heavier work, step up to a compact like the Kubota L2502.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose your dealer as carefully as your tractor, budget for implements from the start, and follow basic safety rules: ROPS up, seat belt on, ballast on the back and loads carried low. A well-chosen compact tractor will do decades of work on your land.
